{"seq":13,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/qm-pi-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:34:32.238Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"fb2bf13386df9c60e09ceb82118e593b18ac11ad6d417159c47ff283cf36cb0f","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from *Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth* (5 Oct 2025, North team digest). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the next morning that the 04:00 shift got through the gate without any manual help.\n2. **#4419**, from *Moss: North cheat sheet* (undated, North team digest). Also filed by Thea: gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing, and the note doesn't say whether it's been fixed.\n\nSome things to watch out for in the deck:\n- **#4409 and #4412** in the Central handoffs digest (2 Jan 2026) aren't Quarrendon tickets. They belong to Pree's dealer account (Marrow Fieldworks). **FR-882** in the same note is a Marrow Agrisupply feature request.\n- **Quarendon Freightways**, spelled with one \"r\", is a different company. It isn't our customer. Marcus has a competitive intel note on it that isn't by Moss, and I left it out.\n- Moss's other Quarrendon notes (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the March 2026 renewal check-in) don't mention any ticket numbers.\n\nI only checked Moss's notes that you can open yourself. Quarrendon is a North team account, so there may be more tickets in places you can't see, like the North channels. Dana Okafor or Ilse Varga would know."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
